      "dom_id": "question-71061",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{3}-4$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{3}-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-5(3{x}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-15{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
